\section*{Rational injectivity of reduced coarse assembly}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For a uniformly discrete bounded-geometry union of finite graphs, an infinite-order degree-one coarse K-homology class is claimed to have zero ordinary reduced assembly image, contradicting coarse Novikov injectivity. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} For some uniformly discrete bounded-geometry coarse disjoint union $X$ of finite connected uniformly bounded-degree graphs, OpenAI claims an infinite-order $\alpha\in KX_1(X)$ with
\[
\mu_X(\alpha)=0\in K_1(C^*(X)).
\]
The target is the ordinary reduced Roe algebra and $KX$ is coarse topological $K$-homology. Consequently ordinary coarse assembly is not injective integrally or after rational tensoring. Bounded geometry means each fixed-radius ball has uniformly bounded cardinality.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 307, 2026-09-23): Congruence fibers over growing triangular discs become trivial on their boundary cycles. Short-loop control keeps boundary winding alive through every fixed Rips scale, independently of the index argument. Uniform approximation of constant-fiber projections constructs a Roe-algebra transfer with the exact boundary restriction; the filled base disc then kills the analytic image of that persistent class.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 307, 2026-09-23): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed counterexample to that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 307, the scope page documents the following selections. The ordinary reduced coarse-assembly selection uses a bounded-degree graph union and an infinite-order degree-one kernel class. It does not select the later maximal-completion argument. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. Its selected declaration also covers the clause used for this problem. Comparator files: CoarseAssembly.lean. Declarations: OAI.CoarseAssembly.bounded\_geometry\_graph\_counterexample\_unconditional.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

